      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused imports (`assertFalse`, `assertTrue`, `StringUtils`)\n- Unused constant `NUL`\n- The `checkReadEof` helper's purpose (verifying repeated EOF reads after exhaustion) isn't communicated\n\nI'll write an improved version that removes the dead code and makes the intent clearer.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed unused imports (`assertFalse`, `assertTrue`, `StringUtils`) and the unused `NUL` constant, added a Javadoc comment to `checkReadEof` explaining its EOF-stability intent, renamed `reader` to `sequenceReader` for clarity, and added an Arrange/Act+Assert comment structure to guide readers through the test's logic."
